				<div id=3D"bodyContent" class=3D"vector-body" aria-labelledby=3D"firstH=
eading" data-mw-ve-target-container=3D"">
					<div class=3D"vector-body-before-content">
							<div class=3D"mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id=3D"siteSub" class=3D"noprint">From postmarketOS Wiki</div>
					</div>
					<div id=3D"contentSub"><div id=3D"mw-content-subtitle"><span class=3D"=
mw-redirectedfrom">(Redirected from <a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.or=
g/index.php?title=3DUSB_Networking&amp;redirect=3Dno" class=3D"mw-redirect"=
 title=3D"USB Networking">USB Networking</a>)</span></div></div>
				=09
				=09
					<div id=3D"mw-content-text" class=3D"mw-body-content"><div class=3D"mw=
-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang=3D"en" dir=3D"ltr"><p>Out of the box, a=
 postmarketOS device uses a static address of <i>172.16.42.1</i><code>/24</=
code> on any USB network interface and runs the <a rel=3D"nofollow" class=
=3D"external text" href=3D"https://gitlab.postmarketos.org/postmarketOS/unu=
dhcpd">unudhcpd</a> DHCP server, offering one address, 172.16.42.2/24, to t=
he USB network.  After plugging a cable between your device and a PC, from =
the PC you might be able to SSH to the phone with:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>ssh<span class=3D=
"w"> </span>user@172.16.42.1
</pre></div>
<p>This article provides details in case this does not work out of the box =
(no IP assigned, doing a new port, etc.).
</p>
<meta property=3D"mw:PageProp/toc">
<h1><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Connecting">Connecting</span></h1>
<table role=3D"text container" class=3D"icon-box box-note" style=3D"--ib-ba=
ckground: #f6efe5; --ib-background-dark: #261c09; --ib-border-color: #ac660=
0; --ib-border-color-dark: #6a481c; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid;=
 margin: 4px 0; border-collapse: collapse;"><tbody><tr>
<td style=3D"padding: 2px 0 2px 0.9em; text-align: center; line-height: 1;"=
><span style=3D"white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span title=
=3D"Note"><img alt=3D"Note" src=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/images/6/6=
d/Reference_icon.svg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"20" height=3D"20" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span></span></span></td>
<td style=3D"padding: 0.35em 0.9em; width: 100%;"><b>Note:</b> If you have =
multiple postmarketOS devices connected, you may want to manually set IP vi=
a <code>setup-interfaces</code> both on host and on second phone to <code>1=
72.16.42.x</code> (or any other) to have internet access on all devices.</t=
d>
</tr></tbody></table>
<p>Power on your device and connect it to your USB port. A new network inte=
rface should appear, run <code>ip a</code> to list all of them. The new ent=
ry should look something like:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>ip<span class=3D"=
w"> </span>a
<span class=3D"go">1: enp0s19f2u1: &lt;BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP&gt; =
mtu 1500 qdisc fq_codel state UNKNOWN group default qlen 1000</span>
<span class=3D"go">    link/ether aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff</=
span>
<span class=3D"go">    inet 172.16.42.2/24 brd 172.16.42.255 scope global d=
ynamic noprefixroute enp0s19f2u1</span>
<span class=3D"go">       valid_lft 861920sec preferred_lft 861920sec</span=
>
<span class=3D"go">    inet6 fe80::aabb:ccdd:eeff:00aa/64 scope link nopref=
ixroute</span>
<span class=3D"go">       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever</span>
</pre></div>
<p>If you instead get something like -
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>ip<span class=3D"=
w"> </span>a
<span class=3D"go">5: enp4s0u1u1: &lt;BROADCAST,MULTICAST&gt; mtu 1500 qdis=
c noop state DOWN group default qlen 1000</span>
<span class=3D"go">    link/ether 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff</=
span>
</pre></div>
<p>then you need to give the interface a proper MAC address to be able to g=
et an IP address, run <code>sudo ip link set dev enp4s0u1u1 address 12:12:1=
2:12:12:12</code>. Make sure you specify the right interface name.
</p><p>You should now have been assigned the IP address <code>172.16.42.2</=
code> (verify with <code>ip a</code> or <code>ifconfig</code>). If it still=
 does not work automatically, you might need to run a DHCP client on your P=
C (<code>dhclient</code> or <code>dhcpcd</code>).
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"SSH">SSH</span></h2>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
79875"><table role=3D"text container" class=3D"icon-box box-note" style=3D"=
--ib-background: #f6efe5; --ib-background-dark: #261c09; --ib-border-color:=
 #ac6600; --ib-border-color-dark: #6a481c; border-width: 1px; border-style:=
 solid; margin: 4px 0; border-collapse: collapse;"><tbody><tr>
<td style=3D"padding: 2px 0 2px 0.9em; text-align: center; line-height: 1;"=
><span style=3D"white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span title=
=3D"Note"><img alt=3D"Note" src=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/images/6/6=
d/Reference_icon.svg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"20" height=3D"20" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span></span></span></td>
<td style=3D"padding: 0.35em 0.9em; width: 100%;">There is a dedicated arti=
cle for <a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Inspecting_the_initra=
mfs" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Inspecting the initramfs">inspecting th=
e initramfs</a> via telnet.</td>
</tr></tbody></table>
<p>When you are past the initramfs, you should be able to connect via <code=
>ssh</code> and the username and password you set during the install phase:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>ssh<span class=3D=
"w"> </span>user@172.16.42.1
<span class=3D"go">user@172.16.42.1's password: </span>
<span class=3D"go">Welcome to postmarketOS!</span>

<span class=3D"go">This distribution is based on Alpine Linux.</span>
<span class=3D"go">Read both our wikis to find a large amount of how-to gui=
des and</span>
<span class=3D"go">general information about administrating and development=
.</span>
<span class=3D"go">See &lt;https://wiki.postmarketos.org&gt; and &lt;https:=
//wiki.alpinelinux.org&gt;.</span>

<span class=3D"go">You may change this message by editing /etc/motd.</span>

<span class=3D"gp">localhost:~$</span>
</pre></div>
<p>Use <code>sudo</code> to run commands as <code>root</code>, it is config=
ured.
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Prevent_host_key_verification_clashes=
_when_connecting_to_different_devices">Prevent host key verification clashe=
s when connecting to different devices</span></h3>
<p>If you have multiple devices you want to SSH into, you will get issues w=
ith host key verification as your system will realize it's talking to diffe=
rent devices on the same IP address. To prevent this, disable host key veri=
fication entirely for the IP address used by postmarketOS devices when conn=
ected by USB.
</p><p>Add the following to <code>~/.ssh/config</code>:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"lt=
r"><pre><span></span>Host pmos
    HostName 172.16.42.1
    UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null
    StrictHostKeyChecking no
</pre></div>
<p>Afterwards you can connect to your device by running <code>ssh &lt;usern=
ame&gt;@pmos</code>. Replace <code>&lt;username&gt;</code> with the proper =
username on your device.
</p>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
79875"><table role=3D"text container" class=3D"icon-box box-note" style=3D"=
--ib-background: #f6efe5; --ib-background-dark: #261c09; --ib-border-color:=
 #ac6600; --ib-border-color-dark: #6a481c; border-width: 1px; border-style:=
 solid; margin: 4px 0; border-collapse: collapse;"><tbody><tr>
<td style=3D"padding: 2px 0 2px 0.9em; text-align: center; line-height: 1;"=
><span style=3D"white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span title=
=3D"Note"><img alt=3D"Note" src=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/images/6/6=
d/Reference_icon.svg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"20" height=3D"20" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span></span></span></td>
<td style=3D"padding: 0.35em 0.9em; width: 100%;">You can also add <code>Us=
er &lt;username&gt;</code> to <code>~/.ssh/config</code> in order to not ha=
ve to enter your username everytime!</td>
</tr></tbody></table>
<h2><span id=3D"Share_device_TCP.2FIP_ports_through_the_PC"></span><span cl=
ass=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Share_device_TCP/IP_ports_through_the_PC">Share d=
evice TCP/IP ports through the PC</span></h2>
<p>To share ports from the <i>postmarketOS</i> device through a computer, d=
o this:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>socat<span class=
=3D"w"> </span>tcp-listen:<span class=3D"o">[</span>OUTWARD<span class=3D"w=
"> </span>PORT<span class=3D"o">]</span>,reuseaddr,fork<span class=3D"w"> <=
/span>tcp:<span class=3D"o">[</span>DEVICE<span class=3D"w"> </span>IP<span=
 class=3D"w"> </span>ADDRESS<span class=3D"o">]</span>:<span class=3D"o">[<=
/span>INWARD<span class=3D"w"> </span>DEVICE<span class=3D"w"> </span>PORT<=
span class=3D"o">]</span>
</pre></div>
<p>For SSH, <i>[INWARD DEVICE PORT]</i> is <i>22</i>.
</p><p><i>[OUTWARD PORT]</i> can be <i>90</i>XX when connected to <i>adb</i=
> (Android Debug Bridge tool) to open the socket port using Android with co=
nnection forwarding - <code>adb reverse </code> (or) <code>adb forward </co=
de> - with <code>tcp:[PORT] tcp:[PORT]</code>.
</p>
<h2><span id=3D"Add_IP_addresses_to_the_Alpine_Linux_device.27s_network_int=
erfaces"></span><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Add_IP_addresses_to_the_A=
lpine_Linux_device's_network_interfaces">Add IP addresses to the Alpine Lin=
ux device's network interfaces</span></h2>
<p>To use networks from other computers, editing <i>/etc/network/interfaces=
</i> can be needed.
</p><p>To put IP information into that, you can do:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span><span class=3D"nb=
">echo</span><span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"s1">$'echo -e \'[line=
 of file]\' &gt;&gt; /etc/network/interfaces'</span><span class=3D"w"> </sp=
an><span class=3D"p">|</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>sudo<span class=3D"w=
"> </span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"nv">$SHELL</span><span =
class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>-s
</pre></div>
<p>and use the page <a rel=3D"nofollow" class=3D"external text" href=3D"htt=
ps://wiki.alpinelinux.org/wiki/Configure_Networking#IPv4_DHCP_Configuration=
">Configure Networking - Alpine Linux (IPv4 DHCP Configuration)</a>.
</p>
<h1><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</spa=
n></h1>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Try_IPv4_only">Try IPv4 only</span></=
h2>
<p>Especially while mainlining, getting an IP often only works with the fol=
lowing command:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>dhcpcd<span class=
=3D"w"> </span>interface<span class=3D"w"> </span>--nohook<span class=3D"w"=
> </span>ipv6
</pre></div>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Making_sure_the_USB_is_detected">Maki=
ng sure the USB is detected</span></h2>
<p>In case you don't get an IP address directly, make sure that your PC rec=
ognizes the phone after it booted into postmarketOS at all. It should show =
the following in <code>dmesg</code>.
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-dmesg mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"l=
tr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"m">[ 6284.442088] </span><span class=
=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> new high-speed USB device number 36 using xhci_hcd
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.627106] </span><span class=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> N=
ew USB device found, idVendor=3D18d1, idProduct=3Dd001
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.627123] </span><span class=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> N=
ew USB device strings: Mfr=3D1, Product=3D2, SerialNumber=3D3
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.627134] </span><span class=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> P=
roduct: Android
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.627143] </span><span class=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> M=
anufacturer: Android
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.627151] </span><span class=3D"k">usb 1-1:</span> S=
erialNumber: 0123456789ABCDEF
<span class=3D"m">[ 6284.632322] </span><span class=3D"k">rndis_host 1-1:</=
span>1.0 usb0: register 'rndis_host' at usb-0000:00:14.0-1, RNDIS device, b=
2:c4:1e:03:64:b9
<span class=3D"m">[ 6285.239048] </span><span class=3D"k">rndis_host 1-1:</=
span>1.0 enp0s20f0u1: renamed from usb0
<span class=3D"m">[ 6285.287058] </span><span class=3D"k">IPv6:</span> ADDR=
CONF(NETDEV_UP): enp0s20f0u1: link is not ready
</pre></div>
<p>It should also show up on <code>lsusb</code> (the name doesn't necessari=
ly match the model):
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"lt=
r"><pre><span></span>Bus 001 Device 023: ID 18d1:d001 Google Inc. Nexus 4 (=
fastboot)
Bus 001 Device 001: ID 1d6b:0002 Linux Foundation 2.0 root hub
Bus 005 Device 001: ID 1d6b:0001 Linux Foundation 1.1 root hub
</pre></div>
<p>And <code>ip link</code> should show an additional entry as well (the la=
st one, in the following list):
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"lt=
r"><pre><span></span>1: lo: &lt;LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP&gt; mtu 65536 qdisc no=
queue state UNKNOWN mode DEFAULT group default qlen 1
    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00
2: enp3s0: &lt;BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP&gt; mtu 1500 qdisc fq_codel =
state UP mode DEFAULT group default qlen 1000
    link/ether e2:88:85:58:0f:99 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff
3: wlp2s0: &lt;BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP&gt; mtu 1500 qdisc mq state =
UP mode DORMANT group default qlen 1000
    link/ether e2:08:85:58:0f:99 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff
14: enp0s29f7u3: &lt;BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP&gt; mtu 1500 qdisc fq_=
codel state UNKNOWN mode DEFAULT group default qlen 1000
    link/ether 86:11:85:5e:df:fa brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff
</pre></div>
<p>If that's the case and you can't connect, your computer probably just do=
esn't have an IP address on its side of the link.
</p><p>If however, nothing shows up (even when <a href=3D"https://wiki.post=
marketos.org/wiki/Inspecting_the_initramfs" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"=
Inspecting the initramfs">Inspecting the initramfs</a>), the most likely re=
ason is a wrong <a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Kernel_config=
uration" title=3D"Kernel configuration">Kernel_configuration</a>. This is h=
ighly device-specific, but some hints can be found in <a href=3D"https://wi=
ki.postmarketos.org/wiki/USB_Network#Kernel_configuration_parameters">#Kern=
el configuration parameters</a>
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"No_IP_assigned_or_MAC_address_is_00:0=
0:00:00:00:00">No IP assigned or MAC address is 00:00:00:00:00:00</span></h=
2>
<p>If USB gets detected, then you probably don't have a network manager tha=
t automatically requests IP addresses from new ethernet interfaces, so you'=
ll have to set the interface up manually.
</p><p>If there's no MAC address assigned(00:00:00:00:00:00), you need to a=
ssign one.
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp"># </span>ip<span class=3D"=
w"> </span>link<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"nb">set</span><span=
 class=3D"w"> </span>dev<span class=3D"w"> </span>enp0s20f0u1<span class=3D=
"w"> </span>address<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"m">12</span>:12=
:12:12:12:12
</pre></div>
<p>Use the following command to start a DHCP client. Replace the interface =
name with the one on your machine (see <code>ip a</code> before and after c=
onnecting the device via USB). Some Linux distributions have <code>dhcpcd</=
code> installed instead of <code>dhclient</code>.
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>dhclient<span cla=
ss=3D"w"> </span>-v<span class=3D"w"> </span>enp0s20f0u1
</pre></div>
<p>Some distribution use other tools that might interfere with <code>dhclie=
nt</code> and <code>dhcpcd</code>. In most cases, you should be able to set=
 an IP address with
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp"># </span>ip<span class=3D"=
w"> </span>address<span class=3D"w"> </span>add<span class=3D"w"> </span>de=
v<span class=3D"w"> </span>enp0s20f0u1<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=
=3D"m">172</span>.16.42.2/24
</pre></div>
<p>If after assigning an IP address and <code>ip a</code> shows your device=
 status as "DOWN" instead of "UNKNOWN", bring it up with=20
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp"># </span>ip<span class=3D"=
w"> </span>link<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"nb">set</span><span=
 class=3D"w"> </span>enp0s20f0u1<span class=3D"w"> </span>up
</pre></div>
<p><br>
P.S. If your device is Samsung with old kernel and <code>CONFIG_USB_ANDROID=
_SAMSUNG_COMPOSITE</code>, something like <a rel=3D"nofollow" class=3D"exte=
rnal text" href=3D"https://gitlab.postmarketos.org/postmarketOS/pmaports/-/=
blob/master/device/unmaintained/linux-samsung-klte-downstream/0007-usb_gadg=
et-set-random-rndis-host-MAC-address-to-prev.patch">usb_gadget-set-random-r=
ndis-host-MAC-address.patch</a> can help with preventing zero MAC.
</p><p>After the interface is brought up you can SSH to the phone at the ph=
one's ip address:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-shell-session mw-content-ltr" =
dir=3D"ltr"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"gp"># </span>ssh<span class=3D=
"w"> </span>user@172.16.42.1
<span class=3D"go">username here is dependent on what you chose in the pmbo=
otstrap init step</span>
</pre></div>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Kernel_configuration_parameters">Kern=
el configuration parameters</span></h2>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
79875"><table role=3D"text container" class=3D"icon-box box-note" style=3D"=
--ib-background: #f6efe5; --ib-background-dark: #261c09; --ib-border-color:=
 #ac6600; --ib-border-color-dark: #6a481c; border-width: 1px; border-style:=
 solid; margin: 4px 0; border-collapse: collapse;"><tbody><tr>
<td style=3D"padding: 2px 0 2px 0.9em; text-align: center; line-height: 1;"=
><span style=3D"white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span title=
=3D"Note"><img alt=3D"Note" src=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/images/6/6=
d/Reference_icon.svg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"20" height=3D"20" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span></span></span></td>
<td style=3D"padding: 0.35em 0.9em; width: 100%;">Outdated. PostmarketOS us=
es NCM now.</td>
</tr></tbody></table>
<p>If you think that the kernel configuration may be at fault, first double=
 check with <code>pmbootstrap kconfig check</code> that the required parame=
ters are all set.
The postmarketOS initramfs is able to configure two different USB systems i=
n the kernel in order to let your PC talk to your phone via networking. One=
 of them has to be enabled (exclusively?):
</p>
<ul><li><a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Kernel_configuration/=
Specific_options#CONFIG_USB_ETH" title=3D"Kernel configuration/Specific opt=
ions">CONFIG_USB_ETH</a>
<ul><li><a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Kernel_configuration/=
Specific_options#CONFIG_USB_ETH_RNDIS" title=3D"Kernel configuration/Specif=
ic options">CONFIG_USB_ETH_RNDIS</a> is usually needed as well, it enables =
a compatibility interface for microsoft hosts.</li>
<li>Usually used in mainline kernels (see also: <a href=3D"https://wiki.pos=
tmarketos.org/wiki/Mainlining_FAQ" title=3D"Mainlining FAQ">Mainlining FAQ<=
/a>)</li></ul></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Kernel_configuration/Spec=
ific_options#CONFIG_USB_G_ANDROID" title=3D"Kernel configuration/Specific o=
ptions">CONFIG_USB_G_ANDROID</a>
<ul><li>This option is usually enabled in Android kernel forks</li></ul></l=
i></ul>
<p>You can use <code>grep</code> on your kernel config to check which of th=
ese options are enabled or not (<code>option=3Dy</code> means it is enabled=
). If you want to change the options, don't modify the file directly, but u=
se <code>pmbootstrap kconfig edit</code> (<a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarke=
tos.org/wiki/Kernel_configuration" title=3D"Kernel configuration">usage ins=
tructions</a>). Otherwise the dependencies in that configuration file will =
not get resolved properly and cause other issues.
</p><p>Related: <a rel=3D"nofollow" class=3D"external text" href=3D"https:/=
/gitlab.postmarketos.org/postmarketOS/pmbootstrap/-/merge_requests/1462">!1=
462</a> linux-postmarketos-qcom: Remove composite usb gadget for networking
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"SSH_issues">SSH issues</span></h2>
<p>If SSH doesn't work for one reason or another, you can try enabling teln=
etd on your installation. For that, add the debug-shell initfs hook and con=
nect to it. Then run the following commands to mount your root partition (w=
ritable):
</p>
<pre>source /etc/deviceinfo
source init_functions.sh
mount_root_partition
mount -o rw,remount /sysroot
</pre>
<p>Put the following content into <code>/sysroot/etc/init.d/telnetd</code>:
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-bash mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"lt=
r"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"ch">#!/sbin/openrc-run</span>

<span class=3D"nv">command</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D=
"s2">"/usr/sbin/telnetd"</span>
<span class=3D"nv">command_args</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span cla=
ss=3D"s2">"-F"</span>
<span class=3D"nv">pidfile</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D=
"s2">"/run/</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">RC_SVCNAME=
</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">.pid"</span>
<span class=3D"nv">command_background</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><sp=
an class=3D"s2">"yes"</span>

depend<span class=3D"o">()</span><span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"o=
">{</span>
<span class=3D"w">        </span>need<span class=3D"w"> </span>net<span cla=
ss=3D"w"> </span>localmount
<span class=3D"w">        </span>after<span class=3D"w"> </span>firewall
<span class=3D"o">}</span>
</pre></div>
<p>Then make the file executable and enable the service so telnet gets laun=
ched by openrc:
</p>
<pre>chmod +x /sysroot/etc/init.d/telnetd &amp;&amp; chroot /sysroot rc-upd=
ate add telnetd default
</pre>
<p>Then resume boot by typing <code>pmos_continue_boot</code>. Telnetd shou=
ld be started once the device boots and you should be able to connect to it=
.
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Using_Dropbear">Using Dropbear</span>=
</h3>
<p>Alternatively you can try to use <code>dropbear</code> SSH server instea=
d of default <code>openssh</code>. For this you can avoid messing with debu=
g-shell hook and modifying system on running phone, you can tweak rootfs be=
fore flashing it in this sequence:
</p>
<pre>1. pmbootstrap init
2. pmbootstrap install
3. pmbootstrap chroot -r    # go inside you phone's future rootfs
4. # make modifications to rootfs
   # in this case, to workaround an SSH issue:
   apk add dropbear
   rc-update del sshd default
   rc-update add dropbear default
5. exit
6. pmbootstrap install      # again, to recreate image
   # flash images as usual
7. pmbootstrap flasher flash_kernel
8. pmbootstrap flasher flash_rootfs
</pre>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Note_about_HTC_devices">Note about HT=
C devices</span></h2>
<ul><li>HTC devices seem to be tricky in general, we have a <a href=3D"http=
s://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Troubleshooting:boot#See_also" class=3D"mw-r=
edirect" title=3D"Troubleshooting:boot">few open issues</a> with HTC device=
s that seem to be not booting</li>
<li>The <a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/HTC_Desire_(htc-bravo=
)" title=3D"HTC Desire (htc-bravo)">HTC desire</a> does work, and it requir=
ed <a rel=3D"nofollow" class=3D"external text" href=3D"https://gitlab.postm=
arketos.org/postmarketOS/pmbootstrap/-/blob/bd4ebb3473764108daa92b308511be7=
e0a1b6948/aports/device/device-htc-bravo/initfs-hook.sh#L8">this line in th=
e initfs-hook</a> to get USB network</li>
<li>It was hard to discover: drebrez used the <a href=3D"https://wiki.postm=
arketos.org/wiki/Tuning_sysfs" title=3D"Tuning sysfs">tuning sysfs</a> inst=
ructions, but he had to write it as a initfs hook and save it in the <code>=
cache</code> partition of the device, then reboot in TWRP to get that file.=
</li>
<li>Without a working display, no USB network and no serial output, you can=
 use the LEDs for debugging and the other partitions to store files.</li></=
ul>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Windows_driver">Windows driver</span>=
</h2>
<p>See <a href=3D"https://wiki.postmarketos.org/wiki/Windows_FAQ#USB_networ=
king" title=3D"Windows FAQ">Windows_FAQ#USB_networking</a>.
</p>
